WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.339 --> 00:00:07.570
Biden's campaign platform is 564 pages long.
When those flying ponies collide

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:13.565
with the marzipan rainbows and pixie dust starts to gum up the works of society,

00:00:13.565 --> 00:00:14.922
we're going to be in for a mess.

00:00:14.922 --> 00:00:20.918
On the other hand, I think we're done with this experiment of having the inmates run the asylum.

00:00:20.918 --> 00:00:22.867
PJ O'Rourke is not happy.

00:00:22.867 --> 00:00:26.096
I'm appalled by the choice that we have been
delivered.

00:00:26.096 --> 00:00:30.270
The 72-year-old political humorist, who cut
his teeth writing for the National Lampoon,

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:33.813
and is author of Parliament of Whores, as
well as other bestsellers,

00:00:33.813 --> 00:00:37.750
is back with a new collection of essays, A Cry From The Far Middle.

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:42.000
As you might expect, the book is filled with comic observations on Republicans, Democrats,

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.007
socialism, nationalism, occupational licensing, presidential debates, Twitter, and more.

00:00:47.007 --> 00:00:53.544
But it's hard to hide his lack of optimism, when a book includes quotes like, "This is the end of the world for classical liberalism."

00:00:53.544 --> 00:00:58.533
"I'm betting that human nature will triumph over adversity and challenge. And I don't mean that in a good way."

00:00:58.533 --> 00:01:03.910
And then of course, "we have a gigantic political tumor.  I'm not optimistic about the biopsy."

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:07.251
Are you okay?

00:01:07.251 --> 00:01:14.850
No, I'm not okay any more than any of the
rest of us are at the moment. I am worried.

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:23.664
I have always belonged to the pessimistic
wing of the libertarian attitude.

00:01:23.664 --> 00:01:30.700
There are many libertarians who believe that people are ultimately rational, I am not among them.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:34.340
This is probably because I spent 20 years
as a foreign correspondent,

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:42.000
largely covering wars and insurrections and social upheavals and disturbances of all sorts of ugly cons.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:47.847
I filed from 40-some, 44 countries, none of
them the nice ones.

00:01:47.847 --> 00:01:55.180
Ranging from sort of Lebanon to Bangladesh, to Kosovo, and parts in between.

00:01:55.180 --> 00:02:03.400
And yeah, I'm not sanguined about human beings having a rational—we have a rational side, thank God.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:12.330
And I hope we are appealing to that rational side, but it isn't the only side in our multifaceted,

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:15.300
and sometimes pretty ugly little personalities.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.044
O'Rourke does see some bright spots.

00:02:17.044 --> 00:02:23.884
I think there's been a generally liberal shift in the United States, but I partly mean that in a good way,

00:02:23.884 --> 00:02:27.650
on issues of individual liberty and things like gay marriage and so on.

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:30.723
But he's concerned America has forgotten the benefits of free markets.

00:02:30.723 --> 00:02:34.876
When one side gains, it doesn't necessarily mean another side loses.

00:02:34.876 --> 00:02:43.265
More people seem to be moving into the category
of regarding the economy as a kind of pie,

00:02:43.265 --> 00:02:49.015
sort of pizza pie, where if you have too many
slices, I have to eat the Domino's box.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:51.360
And so, instead of baking more pies,

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:55.334
the tendency is to get out the pie knives and go at each other's throats with them.

00:02:55.334 --> 00:03:01.508
We've degenerated into a tribal shouting match, which is just absolutely not helpful at all.

00:03:01.508 --> 00:03:08.800
And the very fact of tribalism runs contrary to my concept of libertarianism.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:16.172
It's all about individual liberty, individual dignity, and individual responsibility.

00:03:16.172 --> 00:03:21.416
When we fall into quarreling tribes, we are negating all of those things.

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:26.940
And not only am I concerned that government outcomes and political outcomes

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:33.520
will be contrary to libertarianism, but the very basis that these decisions are made upon

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.700
will be contrary to libertarianism,

00:03:35.709 --> 00:03:39.982
is already to a very large extent, contrary to libertarian.

00:03:39.982 --> 00:03:43.583
O'Rourke now finds himself at odds with the
party he once considered his home.

00:03:43.583 --> 00:03:52.635
As I watched the Republicans not resist this
dangerous and unpredictable man, not to mention,

00:03:52.635 --> 00:03:56.595
like rude, divisive, and any number of other
adjectives,

00:03:56.600 --> 00:04:06.980
I went from being sort of a Republican in remission to being to a certain extent, outright hostile to the party,

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:13.140
to tell the truth. I mean, it isn't so much exactly what Trump has done,

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:14.920
there are even some things that he's done,

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:24.000
like lowering the corporate tax rate to the level that is customary in developed countries, that I'm fine with.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:30.740
I hate his stand on immigration, but not all of his policy decisions have been wrong.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:36.687
I think he has raised awareness, as we like
to say these days,

00:04:36.687 --> 00:04:40.488
because that's supposed to be something very positive to raise awareness.

00:04:40.488 --> 00:04:44.180
But I think he's raised awareness that China is not our friend,

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:48.196
that the Chinese leadership does not wish us well.

00:04:48.196 --> 00:04:53.334
So, it's not so much a matter of what he's done, it's a matter of what he can do

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:57.220
as the world's most powerful person, he's a giant toddler.

00:04:57.220 --> 00:05:00.660
And anybody who's raised children will understand this metaphor.

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:07.220
He's a toddler at the top of the stairs. There's that moment when you failed to close the baby gate

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:15.000
and you're down there in the hall and you're looking up the stairs and you see the toddler at the top of the stairs,

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:21.311
and that's the meaning of fear. And with him, we have it every day.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:23.020
As O'Rourke is quick to point out,

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:27.000
every presidential election has been touted as the most important in our lifetime.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:32.793
Always. It's like the weather, "They are calling
it the storm of the century!"

00:05:32.793 --> 00:05:35.197
But this year, is there some truth to it?

00:05:35.197 --> 00:05:40.408
Well, it's a little more important than usual,
yeah, I would say.

00:05:40.408 --> 00:05:42.898
A fair amount more important than usual.

00:05:42.898 --> 00:05:48.403
I know it's unpleasant facing the Biden-Harris ticket, we're going to be in for a mess.

00:05:48.403 --> 00:05:55.420
It's going to be a messy and expensive couple of years. They seem to be wrong, all wrong,

00:05:55.420 --> 00:06:04.064
quite wrong about everything, but wrong within normal parameters of wrong. We've endured wrong before.

00:06:04.064 --> 00:06:08.694
There's wrong and there's damn wrong.

